<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saanen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saanen is a municipality in the canton of Bern, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, in the upper valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarine">Sarine</a> (Saane), and includes the resort of Gstaad. Once part of the County of Gruyère, it passed to Bern when the indebted county was divided in 1555, and its German-speaking inhabitants adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. It is now known for tourism and cheese-making.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saanen.jpg" alt="Saanen" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saanen_Winter.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
